{
  "dom_id": "step-q84488",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "A softball team has a $60%$ chance of winning each game in a $12$-game season. What is the mean number of games that the team wins during a season?",
  "worked_solution": "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of games that the team wins in a given season. \n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=12$ games\n\n- the probability of winning each game is $p=60%=0.6$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(12,0.6).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the mean is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the mean of the number of games won is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\  & =(12)(0.6) \\\\  & =7.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
